  "sourceQuote": "직각삼각형 $\\text{ABC}$에서 $\\angle\\text{C}=90^\\circ$, $\\overline{\\text{BC}}=4$, $",
  "sourceConditions": [
    {
      "id": "q11_solution",
      "condition": "직각삼각형 $\\text{ABC}$에서 $\\angle\\text{C}=90^\\circ$, $\\overline{\\text{BC}}=4$, $\\overline{\\text{AC}}=3$이므로 $$\\overline{\\text{AB}} = \\sqrt{4^2 + 3^2} = 5$$ $\\triangle\\text{BDE}$와 $\\triangle\\text{BAC}$에서 $\\angle\\text{BED}=\\angle\\text{BCA}=90^\\circ$이고 $\\angle\\text{B}$는 공통이므로 $\\triangle\\text{BDE}\\sim\\triangle\\text{BAC}$이다. 따라서 $\\angle\\text{BDE}=\\angle\\text{BAC}=x^\\circ$이므로 $$\\cos x^\\circ = \\cos A = \\frac{\\overline{\\text{AC}}}{\\overline{\\text{AB}}} = \\frac{3}{5}$$ 따라서 정답은 ①이다.",
      "mappedTo": "mathPlan.nodes"
    }
  ],
